Divine energy is the stuff a god is made of. It cannot be created and cannot be destroyed; when a divine being dies its energy leaks out into the surroundings and spreads, the way heat leaves a room. Passed down a line of descendants it only dilutes, which is how the [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessians]] thin and lose it. It works differently from mortal energy, the kind a mortal caster draws on.

[[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]] is unusually rich in it because three gods have bled into the ground there for hundreds of thousands of years, and it can be mined from the soil. A place cut off from the outside world holds what divine energy is released inside it, so a thing killed in a closed room leaves its power there to be gathered up. [[People/Althane/Henrik|Henrik]]'s [[Phenomena/Althane/Divine Amphora|Divine Amphora]] moves it from one vessel to another, and the machinery of [[Geography/Althane/The Thirteenth Realm|the Thirteenth Realm]] draws it from the corpses of the [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessians]] it holds.

The [[Divinity/Althane/The Stranger|Stranger]] was the reverse of a Thessian: he began mortal and burned mortal energy, so he needed others to turn the divine energy of Althane into mortal energy for him.

A god struck with a [[Phenomena/Althane/Godpiercer|godpiercer]] loses all of its divinity at once, which is converted to mortal energy and left in the world as the god is made mortal.
